module contract;

// Card CELL-RESULT-SET-WRITTEN-SET-DERIVATION (contract specification C09.4,
// grammar G05j as amended, gateway rule 38e as amended). The user launched
// the card on 2026-11-04 (verbatim): "CELL-RESULT-SET-WRITTEN-SET-DERIVATION."
//
// USER DECISION 2026-11-04 (verbatim): "Basically, Q1(a) and Q2(i) But we
// must not handle descriptor 0 as a valid handle. So, we need to exclude the
// 0 descriptor like: written_set(pipedes, [1, MAX]); a live descriptor is in
// [1, MAX]". USER DECISION 2026-11-04 (verbatim): "Write [1, MAX]".
//
// `flb_pipe_create` writes both descriptors of its pair in [1, MAX] when it
// returns 0. A bounds contract v1 value set only (rule 38's creation check
// reads it; the bounds consumer and every custody reader do not): no
// custody is stated or changed, and `flb_pipe_create` stays without a
// resource declaration, so no route reads these sets yet.
//
// The sets are DERIVED, not assumed: `quirin-audit pin --bounds
// --derive-results --compile-database FILE` reads the configured unit
// (`src/flb_pipe.c` of Fluent Bit's Linux build) through Clang and derives
// the forwarding `return pipe(pipefd);` (`flb_pipe.c:100`) over the C
// library's declared `pipe` written sets (`quirin-provider-libc`'s
// `libc/result_sets.qv`). The Windows body of the same file (`flb_pipe.c:55`,
// `evutil_socketpair`, which states no written set) derives nothing: each
// configuration's body decides its own set, and the lock records the
// configured unit's.
//
// THE BOUND IS A DECLARED POLICY, NOT POSIX'S SET. The derivation rests on
// `pipe`'s `written_set(pipedes[0|1], [1, MAX])`, the user's declared policy;
// POSIX's set is [0, MAX] and descriptor 0 is observed natively (`ch_data`
// is `pipe2([0, 3])` with standard input closed). Under POSIX's set the same
// body derives [0, MAX] for `pipefd[0]`, which this declaration does not
// contain, and nothing is pinned. Every reading these sets decide is
// attributed to the bound (follow-up CELL-RESULT-SET-DESCRIPTOR-ZERO-POLICY).
extern fn flb_pipe_create(pipefd: ptr<mut, u8>) -> i32
contract {
    requires bounds_contract_v1;
    ensures normal written_set(pipefd[0], [1, MAX]) when #result == 0;
    ensures normal written_set(pipefd[1], [1, MAX]) when #result == 0;
};
